## All UI Bundles

The requirements and conventions below are shared among all UI bundles


requires:
    - bundle.yaml         # includes bundle metadata e.g. tooltip message

optional:
    - icon.png            # for Revit UI icons
    - icon.dark.png       # for Revit UI icons in **Dark mode**
    - lib/                # can include a lib/ directory that hosts modules required by the commands inside this bundle
    - bin/                # can include a bin/ directory that hosts binaries required by the commands inside this bundle

### Bundle Layout Directives

UI bundles can provide directives on how the child bundles should be ordered in Revit UI. Since pyRevit 4.7, the primary method to provide these directives is to use the Bundle File. These directives are defined in the bundle file and are limited to UI bundles only.

<aside>
<img src="https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/secure.notion-static.com/24882e62-94af-420b-a5ee-d45bba735534/ic_01_idea.png" alt="https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/secure.notion-static.com/24882e62-94af-420b-a5ee-d45bba735534/ic_01_idea.png" width="40px" /> See Bundle Layout for  more information about layout directives

</aside>

**Example**

# layout directives are listed in order under `layout` key
layout:
  - Logs
  - -----
  - Unit Tests
  - Bundle Tests
  - Misc Tests[title:Third-Party\nUnit Tests]
  - Debug Dialog Config
